From 69397e97354aa99d564281fd70d08d2308d6247d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ajay Kumar Nandam <ajay.nandam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:23:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6dsp-lpass-clocks: fix off-by-one in clks[]
 array bound

q6dsp_clock_dev_probe() stores each registered clk_hw directly by its
caller-supplied numeric clk_id:

	cc->clks[id] = clk;

with no further bounds enforcement at registration time (the
Q6DSP_MAX_CLK_ID check only runs later, in q6dsp_of_clk_hw_get(), for
DT consumer lookups). struct q6dsp_cc lays clks[Q6DSP_MAX_CLK_ID]
immediately before desc:

	struct q6dsp_cc {
		struct device *dev;
		struct q6dsp_clk *clks[Q6DSP_MAX_CLK_ID];
		const struct q6dsp_clk_desc *desc;
	};

out-of-tree audioreach-kernel's q6prm clock table now registers a vote
clock with clk_id LPASS_HW_LPR_VOTE == 104, matching the historical
Q6DSP_MAX_CLK_ID of 104. Since valid array indices only run 0..103,
writing cc->clks[104] overflows by one element and lands exactly on
the adjacent desc field, clobbering the q6dsp_clk_desc pointer that
holds the lpass_set_clk/lpass_vote_clk/lpass_unvote_clk callbacks with
a stray struct q6dsp_clk * instead.

The corruption is silent until the next clk_prepare()/clk_unprepare()
call on any clock from this provider dereferences the now-bogus
cc->desc and jumps through a garbage function pointer, e.g.:

  Unable to handle kernel execute from non-executable memory
  ...
  lr : clk_vote_q6dsp_block+0x4c/0x68 [snd_q6dsp_common]
  Call trace:
   clk_core_prepare
   clk_prepare
   pm_clk_resume
   lpi_pinctrl_runtime_resume
   ...
   lpi_pinctrl_probe

This reliably hangs boot on every board that shares the q6prm clock
table (not just the board the new vote clock was added for), since
the table is registered unconditionally regardless of which board
actually uses the new entry.

Bump Q6DSP_MAX_CLK_ID to 105 so index 104 is in bounds again.

Fixes: out-of-tree audioreach-kernel use of LPASS_HW_LPR_VOTE (clk_id 104)
Signed-off-by: Ajay Kumar Nandam <ajay.nandam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
index 03838582aead..ab7d20580638 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6dsp-lpass-ports.h>
 #include "q6dsp-lpass-clocks.h"
 
-#define Q6DSP_MAX_CLK_ID			104
+#define Q6DSP_MAX_CLK_ID			105
 #define Q6DSP_LPASS_CLK_ROOT_DEFAULT		0
 
 
